        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Unplug, loosen both rear bolts one turn each while counting, vacuum from both sides, then
            wipe deck and belt underside with isopropyl alcohol on lint-free cloths — working
            centre-outward and changing faces often. Dry fifteen to thirty minutes.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then <a href="/treadmill-belt-lubrication/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">lubricate</a>,
            retension by the same number of turns, and watch the tracking on the first run.
            Twenty minutes annually — six-monthly on carpet — and it is what makes lubrication
            work rather than an alternative to it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
